  "verdict": "benign",
  "basis": [
    "Exact SHA-512 integrity and SHA-1 match the npm registry distribution record for this version.",
    "macOS codesign verifies the CLI, background application and nested permission helper, and Keychain dylib. Developer ID Application: Adi Singh (5LJFSBRY2F); Apple certificate chain.",
    "Extracted all 122 Bun module-table entries (9328954 bytes); 118 code modules and four image assets. Reviewed entrypoint dispatch, device enrollment and proof authentication, local login collection and transfer, remote worker command routing, service installation and updates, and sandbox boundaries. Independently scanned extracted modules.",
    "The permissions helper uses Accessibility and System Events to guide System Settings onboarding; native AppleScript probe and caller/worker allowlist paths were disassembled with Rizin.",
    "The Keychain dylib targets application-scoped records, creates and signs with non-extractable private proof keys, and exports public key representations. No blanket Keychain dump was found.",
    "Background worker services and remote command/desktop operations are product functionality with CLI setup and device authentication. No evidence of a covert unrelated collection destination was found."
  ],
  "sensitive_behavior": {
    "local_logins": "The device CLI defaults --local-logins on for signed-in personal computers, off with API-key authentication. It reads Claude Code, Codex, Grok, OpenCode and Pi local OAuth records.",
    "handoff": "release-entry-mt8swp15.js:N5 calls the imported K5 collector, then G5 (release-entry-7r9df945.js:v), which projects {provider,access,expires} and drops refresh tokens. It sends those current access tokens to the device-proof-authenticated /local-subscription endpoint, with periodic re-reading as credentials rotate.",
    "desktop_credentials": "desktop-local-logins-10t7trrp.js additionally supports a desktop credential-import action reading supported provider API keys from environment/configuration. This remains a sensitive integration capability.",
    "classification_limit": "Vendor identity and a valid signature alone are not proof of safety. The benign judgment also uses the actual authenticated setup, destinations, option/help disclosure, and reviewed data paths. A standalone collector chunk retains the existing suspicious cross-agent credential-store catalog finding; the whole product reports its established integration context."
  },
